<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title><%= title %></title>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <link rel='stylesheet' href='/stylesheets/style.css' />
  <script src="/javascripts/customer.js" defer></script>
</head>
<body>
<h1><%= title %></h1>
<p>Welcome to <%= title %>.   Let's test reading get+post data</p>

<br/><br/>
<b>Traditional Customer Form </b> to test POST request using URI /readCustomerInfoAndRespond
<br/>
<form action="/readCustomerInfoAndRespond" method="post">

  Name: <input type="text" name="name"> </input>
  <br/>
  Email: <input type="text" name="email"> </input>
  <br/>
  <input type="submit" value="Go"/>
</form>

<section class="customer-api" aria-labelledby="customer-api-heading">
  <h2 id="customer-api-heading">Customer Form using REST / JSON</h2>
  <p>This form uses JavaScript fetch() to call /api/customer and shows the response here without reloading.</p>
  <form id="customer-api-form" action="/api/customer" method="post">
    <label for="customer-name">Name</label>
    <input id="customer-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" required>
    <label for="customer-email">Email</label>
    <input id="customer-email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required>
    <button id="customer-submit" type="submit">Submit with fetch</button>
  </form>
  <p id="customer-result" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p>
  <noscript>Enable JavaScript to try the REST form. The traditional forms still work without JavaScript.</noscript>
</section>

<br><br><br>
<hr>

<b>Form to test GET request</b> and reading the data using URI /readNameAndRespond
<br/>
<form action="/readNameAndRespond" method="get">

  Name: <input type="text" name="name"> </input>
  <br/>
  <input type="submit" value="Go"/>
</form>
<br><br><br>
<hr>
<b>Form to test POST request</b> and reading data using URI  /readNameAndRespond
<br/>
<form action="/readNameAndRespond" method="post">

  Name: <input type="text" name="name"> </input>
  <br/>
  <input type="submit" value="Go"/>
</form>



</body>
</html>
